% 24\u03a9 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(field (name \\\"MPN\\\") \\\"FRC0805J240TSD\\\")\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"If the part is physically 24\u03a9, the supercap-bank output node would be loaded far more heavily than intended, causing excessive current and heat. If it is 24k, the BOM and part description are wrong.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.3\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The most likely anomaly is C54, a +5V decoupling capacitor whose value (0.1nF) contradicts its 100nF part description. R36 has a value/description mismatch that is less certain. Most other nets and values appear consistent with the design intent.\"\n}",
